From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0278: front, ultra-wide and macro sensors; sensor restart after the PHY

The ultra wide streamed (op 10) but CSID0 saw nothing through CSIPHY1: the
sensor was started before the receiver, and a D-PHY receiver has to see the
clock lane's LP-11 to HS start. Op 11 now restarts the sensor's stream once
CSIPHY, PPI and CSID are set up (Android programs the PHY first).
Op 10 serves every slot: 1 OV16A1Q (m1 0x10, CSIPHY2, D-PHY 4 lanes,
2304x1728), 2 S5K4H7 (m1 0x2d, CSIPHY1, 4 lanes, 3264x2448), 3 SC202PCS
(m0 0x36, CSIPHY1 with the CSI mux high, one lane, 1600x1200), from a table
of sensors (chip id, init/mode/stream tables, PHY, lanes, settle, CSID
RX_CFG0); op 11 programs one lane + clock (0x81) for the macro. The front and
macro tables join the generated header.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_cam.c        |  91 ++++--
 bsd/dev/sweet_cam_tables.h | 785 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 850 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

